BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 758.9000000000001 Td (- Centre of mass on a line: x_cm=\(sum m_i x_i\)/\(sum m_i\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 747.0000000000001 Td (- Torque magnitude: tau=rF sin\(theta\); rotational equilibrium requires sum tau=0.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 735.1000000000001 Td (- Moment of inertia: I=sum m_i r_i^2; solid disc about centre: I=\(1/2\)MR^2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 723.2000000000002 Td (- Rotational kinetic energy K=\(1/2\)I omega^2; angular momentum L=I omega.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 711.3000000000002 Td (- Angular kinematics: alpha=\(omega-u_omega\)/t; theta=omega_i t+\(1/2\)alpha t^2; theta=\(\(omega_i+omega_f\)/2\)t.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 699.4000000000002 Td (- Rolling without slipping: v=R omega. Parallel-axis theorem: I=I_cm+Md^2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 687.5000000000002 Td (- Angular momentum conservation: I_i omega_i=I_f omega_f when external torque is zero.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 48 675.6000000000003 Td (- Translation: a=F_net/M for the whole system.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 48 663.7000000000003 Td (Use each equation only when its assumptions apply; keep units consistent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 430 24 Td (StudyNest | Page 2 of 4) Tj ET
